course: dictionary
lesson: 8160
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Reserve» is a good example. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning to use. «We reserved a table for four.» Here, reserve means to ask for something to be kept for you.
explain: «Nature reserves protect wild plants and animals.» The words protect wild plants and animals are the clues. So a nature reserve is a special area of land that keeps wildlife safe.
explain: Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the word. «The team kept a reserve on the bench» only makes sense if a reserve is a player who waits to come on.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Reserve» can mean to ask for something to be kept for you, like a table or a seat.
fact: «Reserve» can also mean an extra amount kept in case it is needed, such as money in reserve.
fact: A «nature reserve» is a protected area of land for wild animals and plants.
fact: In sport, a reserve is a player who waits to come on if needed.
exercise: «We reserved a table for four at the café.» What does reserved mean here? | *Kept for us to use later | Broke into small pieces | Moved to the back of the room | Painted bright blue
exercise: «The nature reserve is home to otters and rare birds.» What is a nature reserve? | A kind of tent | A sports team's bench | *A protected area of land for wild animals and plants | A shop that sells plants
exercise: «The reserve sat on the bench, ready to come on if someone got hurt.» What is the reserve? | A bag of spare socks | A seat that is always empty | A tiger in a zoo | *A player who waits to come on if needed
test: «The South China tiger now survives only in zoos and reserves.» What does reserves mean here? | Old cages with no doors | *Protected places where wild animals are kept safe | Stripes on a tiger's back | Shops that sell tiger toys
test: «Mum keeps some money in reserve for emergencies.» What does reserve mean here? | *An extra amount kept in case it is needed | A player who waits to come on | A protected place for animals | To ask for something to be kept for you
exam: Which sentence uses reserve to mean "to ask for something to be kept for you"? | *«We reserved two seats for the show.» | «The reserve team warmed up.» | «Nature reserves protect wild plants.» | «Pandas live in the mountains.»
